  "notes": "Scope accounting (ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-004): all 26 assigned files read in full; nothing removed from scope — skill definitions and allowed-tools grants included per ACTION-REVIEW-SEC-001. No quantified, reproducible exploit found. Examined and dismissed: (1) merge-resolve allowed-tools adds Bash(git merge *), git merge-tree, cherry-pick/rebase --abort, git commit --no-edit — wider than the global merge --ff-only only while the skill is active; all are local, reversible git operations with no boundary crossed and no attacker-controlled input path. (2) skillroutine-create origin: user marker — the casual lockout it feeds (smine-apply / smine-skills / smine-orchestrate, other chunk) is a protection against automated edits to shipped skills on casual installs, not an adversarial boundary; the stamp is written only on newly created skills. Cross-chunk for the station: the lockout's enforcement lives in smine-* skills outside this chunk. (3) foreign-toolchain-pretag.js suggests an unpinned third-party Docker image (amake/innosetup) when dockerized — supply-chain surface, but the workflow is unreachable today (known correctness-MAJ-40-r1) and no exploit is quantifiable. (4) config-ui-fidelity-gate.js / subsystem-grounding.js / foreign-toolchain-pretag.js interpolate dispatcher-built args into agent prompts (buildCmd is executed by the agent) — args are model-emitted by the fronting skill, the agent runs under the same permission gate, no privilege gain. (5) RULE-PLAN-069 commits running-app screenshots under plans/<slug>/design/ui/ — would leak secrets only if a captured UI renders one; no such UI is identifiable from this chunk (cross-chunk check for the station: whether any config-server page renders tokens). (6) fimplement's sync_public.sh exclude assertion is a security-positive guard (known code-style-NIT-186-r1 covers its placement). (7) railroad-review.js cleanup namespace mismatch is known correctness-BLK-29-r1 — leftover worktrees, not a security boundar